The first one looks the most expensive. But I know it's a trick
Be ready for this to be wrong. That's the whole point of this activity. Ok, bring it on.

Check Your Understanding
Why does the French output cost more than the English one, even though they say the same thing? 
French costs more tokens than English because the AI models are trained with mostly English data. 
Translation costs tokens.
What's the relationship between tokens and words? (Hint: it's not 1:1)
Word vs Token = 100 vs 133 (1 token = 3/4 word)
What is a token? (And why is it not the same as a word?)
A token is a small unit of text that is processed by an AI tool/model
What's the difference between input and output tokens?
Input tokens are tokens you put into the AI tool to process. 
Output tokens are tokens AI produces to deliver to you. 
Why does a Dutch company pay more for AI than an American one, even for the same task?
Because the Dutch company will have to pay more for translations. 

